          "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: one four-view orthographic turnaround sheet for reconstruction with local Hunyuan3D multi-view. Create a wide 2048x1024 image with exactly FOUR isolated views of the SAME complete prop, left to right FRONT / LEFT / BACK / RIGHT, with NO written labels. Pure white background, no ground and no cast shadow. Four evenly spaced columns; each whole object including protrusions must fit inside its own column with white margins, never overlap neighboring views. Align baselines and use exactly the same physical scale and height in all views. True orthographic views, no perspective and no three-quarter view.\nStyle: readable moderate-detail hand-painted fantasy FPS environment at Gunfire Reborn game fidelity. Bold chunky solid silhouette, clean gently chamfered faceted planes, two or three large coherent matte color blocks, soft painted gradients and a few restrained edge-wear accents. Neutral even lighting; no photorealism, dense wood grain, tiny cracks or elaborate miniature carving. No text, icon labels, loose floating parts or thin strings. All parts form one coherent assembled prop. Subject: one short heavy foundry slag cart, approximately 2.8 metres wide including wheels, 2.8 metres long and 2.2 metres high. A squat dark charcoal iron rectangular tub with very thick flared sides, broad folded lip and clearly visible solid wall depth, mounted on a compact heavy timber-and-iron chassis. Two very large thick solid wheels, one on each side, fixed to one broad axle; simple recessed wheel faces and broad iron rims, no thin spokes. A stout integrated rear support shoe and the wheels together provide a grounded stable resting stance. A small amount of dark angular solid slag sits firmly inside the tub below its top edge, no glowing fire or loose falling pieces. Large clean aubergine-charcoal metal planes, restrained dull bronze corner straps and muted rust-brown wear; no bright molten lava. Front and rear show tub body and wheels at its sides; left and right show true chassis length and wheel placement. No long handgrips, tow poles, handles, chain, horse, rails or separate props. Keep its volume compact and robust rather than a thin wagon frame.",
